Ducks tie it right back up. Judd Caulfield drives the net and pops Alex Killorn's feed up and over Woll.

As Aaron Cooney said, "Dad Strength" and the Ducks are back even. 3-3.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Flyers go back ahead shorthanded. That's a tough one.

Around a sliding Carlsson, Foerester whips one on net from a sharp angle, and Dostál just lets that one under the stick and pads to put Philly back in front, 3-2.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Ducks finally on the board, and it's Philadelphia's $18 million man Leo Carlsson. His first goal in five games and first 5-on-5 goal since the season opener.

2-1 Flyers, 11:22 P2.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Nick Jensen added to the scratches on the NHL Media Site.

That means Travis Mitchell is officially back in the Ducks blue line. Ducks are 4-1 with him, 0-5 without him. Maybe he was the secret sauce. 🤔

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Nikita Klepov and Frank Vatrano are the healthy scratches for the Ducks in Philadelphia, per the NHL Media Site.

Lukáš Dostál is back in the starter's net.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Tonight's rosters from the NHL Media Site.

Pavel Mintyukov and Jeff Malott are out. Nick Jensen and Nikita Klepov are in. Judd Caulfield is still back in SoCal (birth of child).

